🌦️ Hybrid Quantum Image Classifier
A Hybrid Quantum-Classical Deep Learning system that classifies outdoor scenes into Road, Sky, and Rain using Transfer Learning and Variational Quantum Circuits (VQC).

📌 Overview
Hybrid Quantum Image Classifier is a research-inspired project that combines Deep Learning with Quantum Machine Learning. A pretrained ResNet50 extracts image features which are processed by a Variational Quantum Circuit (VQC) for final classification. The web application allows users to upload outdoor images and receive predictions with confidence scores.


✨ Features
• Hybrid Quantum-Classical Architecture
• Transfer Learning using ResNet50
• Variational Quantum Circuit (VQC)
• Real-time Image Classification
• Modern Responsive UI
• Prediction Confidence
• Drag & Drop Upload
• Research-Oriented Implementation


🧠 Problem Statement
Traditional image classifiers rely on classical neural networks. This project explores integrating quantum circuits with deep learning to investigate hybrid approaches for computer vision.
🎯 Objectives
• Build a Hybrid Quantum AI model
• Integrate Deep Learning with Quantum Computing
• Classify Road, Sky, and Rain scenes
• Develop an interactive web application
• Demonstrate Quantum AI applications


🏗️ System Architecture
Input Image → Image Preprocessing → ResNet50 Feature Extraction → Feature Reduction → Variational Quantum Circuit (PennyLane) → Quantum Measurement → Fully Connected Layer → Final Prediction
⚙️ Tech Stack
Python, PennyLane, PyTorch, ResNet50, Flask, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, OpenCV, Pillow, NumPy, Matplotlib
🧬 Model Pipeline
Upload Image → Resize & Normalize → ResNet50 Feature Extraction → Feature Compression → Quantum State Encoding → VQC Processing → Quantum Measurement → Prediction Layer → Final Classification


